types — Concept page for BAML type syntax, aliases, generic bounds, and associated type bindings.

Syntax:
  type UserId = string
  class Box<T extends Named> {
    value: T
  }
  type NamedIterator = Iterator<Item = string>
  type Item = (TextCursor as Iterator).Item

Use `type` for aliases, `T extends Bound` for generic bounds, `Interface<Assoc = Type>` to constrain an associated type in a type position, and `(Concrete as Interface).Assoc` when a concrete type implements multiple interface instantiations.
